        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "DC susceptibility of 1 shows χMT = 56.30 cm3 mol−1 K at 300 K (1.0 kOe), a minimum of 45.48 cm3 mol−1 K at 13 K, then an increase to 53.20 cm3 mol−1 K at 1.8 K, indicating intramolecular ferromagnetic Dy–Dy interactions. Zero-dc-field AC data show frequency-dependent χ′ and χ″ and SMM-like slow relaxation. Arrhenius fit of the high-T regime gives Ueff = 17.8 K and τ0 = 1.09×10−6 s; Raman+Orbach fitting over the full range gives Ueff = 27.8 K and τ0 = 1.94×10−7 s. Cole–Cole α = 0.27–0.16 at 2–9 K.",
